        "math_academy_id": "q-38532",
        "problem": "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{\u222c}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{x+y}4z\\,dz]dA\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ in the $xy$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le x}.\n$$",
        "worked_solution": "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z,$ treating $x$ and $y$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{x+y}4z\\,dz]dA & ={\u222c}_{D}[2{z}^{2}]_{z=0}^{z=x+y}\\,dA \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{D}2((x+y)^{2}-0)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{D}2{x}^{2}+4xy+2{y}^{2}\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the double integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{D}2{x}^{2}+4xy+2{y}^{2}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}2{x}^{2}+4xy+2{y}^{2}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}2{x}^{2}+4xy+2{y}^{2}\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[2{x}^{2}y+2x{y}^{2}+\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=x}dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2{x}^{2}(x-0)+2x({x}^{2}-0)+\\frac{2}{3}({x}^{3}-0)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{14}{3}{x}^{3}\\,dx \\\\  & ={[\\frac{7}{6}{x}^{4}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{6}({1}^{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
